From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: Bump gix 0.81.0 -> 0.88.0 for the gix-pack security fixes

gix-pack below 0.75.0 parses pack files unsafely: a crafted pack can
assert on the pack-version-3 header (CVE-2026-109349), misresolve an
ofs-delta base distance (CVE-2026-109350) or exhaust memory on the
header object count (CVE-2026-109351) (boo#1285151).  gix pins its
gix-pack in lockstep (0.81.0 wants ^0.68.0, 0.88.0 wants ^0.75.0), so
the manifest has to move for the lockfile to reach the fixed
gix-pack 0.75.0.  The matching Cargo.lock ships inside vendor.tar.zst.

Downstream security backport, not suitable for upstream submission.

--- a/codex-rs/Cargo.toml
+++ b/codex-rs/Cargo.toml
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@
 flate2 = "1.1.8"
 futures = { version = "0.3", default-features = false }
 gethostname = "1.1.0"
-gix = { version = "0.81.0", default-features = false, features = ["sha1"] }
+gix = { version = "0.88.0", default-features = false, features = ["sha1"] }
 gix-url = "0.35.2"
 glob = "0.3"
 globset = "0.4"
